      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two commit message issues:\n\n1. **Bundled changes (`\"and also save SHCSR\"`):** The subject line (`zephyr: panic: save the active exception number in IPSR`) only describes the `IPSR` fix, while the second paragraph adds `\"and also save SHCSR\"` without explaining the motivation for saving `SHCSR`, and the commit message omits the `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` `esf_placeholder` test addition in `zephyr/test/drivers/panic/src/panic.c`.\n2. **Update after splitting:** Please split the independent changes into separate CLs and use the corresponding commit messages below.\n\n### Option A: Commit messages for the split CLs (Recommended)\n\n**CL 1 (Save active exception number in `IPSR`):**\n```text\nzephyr: panic: save the active exception number in IPSR\n\npanic_data_write_esf() stored the stacked xPSR in the IPSR slot. The\nIPSR field of a stacked xPSR holds the exception number of the\ninterrupted context, which is 0 for faults taken from thread mode, and\nZephyr also clears it for non-nested faults. As a result, panicinfo\nreported \"EXCEPTION: 00\" for CPU faults.\n\nSave the active exception number with __get_IPSR() instead, as legacy\ncros-ec does. The full stacked xPSR is still saved in the exception\nframe.\n\nBUG\u003db:573760632\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.panic.ro\n     -s drivers.panic.rw -s drivers.panic_output.ro\n     -s drivers.panic_output.rw -s drivers.panic_output.ec_host_cmd\n     -s drivers.panic_reason -s drivers.panic_log.minimal\n     -s drivers.panic_log.immediate\nTEST\u003dzmake build r2d2\n\nChange-Id: Iba726c561b8d431a3f2a382ad4ab4276b31692cc\n```\n\n**CL 2 (Save `SHCSR` in Cortex-M panic data):**\n```text\nzephyr: panic: save SHCSR on Cortex-M mainline\n\nZephyr does not include SCB-\u003eSHCSR in struct __extra_esf_info, leaving\ncm.shcsr unpopulated in panic_data on Cortex-M mainline targets.\n\nSave SCB-\u003eSHCSR via CORTEX_PANIC_SYS_REG_LIST when\nCONFIG_ARMV7_M_ARMV8_M_MAINLINE is enabled so panicinfo reports the\nsystem handler control and state register.\n\nBUG\u003db:573760632\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.panic.ro\n     -s drivers.panic.rw\nTEST\u003dzmake build r2d2\n```\n\n**CL 3 (Verify `esf_placeholder` in POSIX `test_panic_data_write_esf`):**\n```text\nzephyr: test: verify POSIX ESF copy in test_panic_data_write_esf\n\ntest_panic_data_write_esf() passed a zero-initialized struct arch_esf\nand only checked header fields populated by panic_data_reset() and\npanic_data_finalize().\n\nSet esf.dummy on CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX and assert that\npanic_data_write_esf() copies it to pdata-\u003eposix.esf_placeholder.\n\nBUG\u003db:573760632\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.panic.ro\n     -s drivers.panic.rw\n```\n\n### Option B: If keeping `IPSR` and `SHCSR` in a single CL\n\n```text\nzephyr: panic: save live Cortex-M IPSR and SHCSR in panic data\n\npanic_data_write_esf() stored the stacked xPSR in the IPSR slot and\nleft cm.shcsr unpopulated because Zephyr does not include SHCSR in\nextra_info. The IPSR field of a stacked xPSR holds the exception\nnumber of the interrupted context (0 in thread mode, and cleared by\nZephyr for non-nested faults), causing panicinfo to report\n\"EXCEPTION: 00\" for CPU faults.\n\nRead the active exception number with __get_IPSR() and capture\nSCB-\u003eSHCSR on Cortex-M mainline targets via CORTEX_PANIC_SYS_REG_LIST,\nmatching legacy cros-ec. The full stacked xPSR remains saved in the\nexception frame.\n\nBUG\u003db:573760632\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.panic.ro\n     -s drivers.panic.rw -s drivers.panic_output.ro\n     -s drivers.panic_output.rw -s drivers.panic_output.ec_host_cmd\n     -s drivers.panic_reason -s drivers.panic_log.minimal\n     -s drivers.panic_log.immediate\nTEST\u003dzmake build r2d2\n\nChange-Id: Iba726c561b8d431a3f2a382ad4ab4276b31692cc\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/84adf0a1-0b27-4ff3-b51d-27eb83e9e93b)",
