      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n* **Functionality:** ✅ Saving `__get_IPSR()` into `cm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR]` instead of the stacked `esf-\u003ebasic.xpsr` properly records the active fault exception number when `panic_data_write_esf()` runs in handler mode, while keeping `esf-\u003ebasic.xpsr` in `cm.frame[CORTEX_PANIC_FRAME_REGISTER_PSR]`. Updating `docs/panic_data.md` matches the new `PANIC_REG_LIST` print order.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Extending `PANIC_REG_LIST` with `PANIC_SYS_REG` / `CORTEX_PANIC_SYS_REG_LIST` and `_VAL` macro variants cleanly integrates live CMSIS register reads alongside ESF field copies in `zephyr/shim/src/panic.c`.\n* **Code Simplicity:** ✅ The macro definitions (`PANIC_SYS_REG`, `PANIC_COPY_REGS_VAL`, and `PANIC_PRINT_REGS_VAL`) are concise and minimal.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ Uses standard CMSIS intrinsics (`__get_IPSR()`, `SCB-\u003eSHCSR`), existing `CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR` enum constants, and appropriate `#if defined(CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M)` / `#if defined(CONFIG_ARMV7_M_ARMV8_M_MAINLINE)` guards.\n* **Security:** ✅ No security concerns.\n* **Testing:** ❌ `test_panic_data_write_esf` in `zephyr/test/drivers/panic/src/panic.c` only adds a `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` assertion (`esf.dummy` -\u003e `pdata-\u003eposix.esf_placeholder`), which exercises the pre-existing POSIX `PANIC_COPY_REGS` macro rather than the Cortex-M `IPSR` fix. Please add Cortex-M test assertions verifying that `pdata-\u003ecm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR]` captures `__get_IPSR()` rather than `esf.basic.xpsr` (see inline comment on `zephyr/test/drivers/panic/src/panic.c`).\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ❌ While the CL is `Size: S (+39, -7)`, it bundles three independently revertible changes across `zephyr/shim/src/panic.c`, `docs/panic_data.md`, and `zephyr/test/drivers/panic/src/panic.c`. Please split this CL into self-contained changes:\n  1. **CL 1:** Save the active exception number with `__get_IPSR()` in `cm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR]` via `PANIC_SYS_REG` / `CORTEX_PANIC_SYS_REG_LIST` in `zephyr/shim/src/panic.c`, update the `ipsr` line position in `docs/panic_data.md`, and add Cortex-M `IPSR` test assertions.\n  2. **CL 2:** Save and print `SCB-\u003eSHCSR` (`cm.shcsr`) via `CORTEX_PANIC_SYS_REG_SHCSR` on `CONFIG_ARMV7_M_ARMV8_M_MAINLINE` in `zephyr/shim/src/panic.c` and add the `shcsr` line to `docs/panic_data.md`.\n  3. **CL 3:** Add the `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` `esf.dummy` / `pdata-\u003eposix.esf_placeholder` verification in `zephyr/test/drivers/panic/src/panic.c`.\n* **Commit Message:** ❌ The subject line (`zephyr: panic: save the active exception number in IPSR`) omits the `SHCSR` addition mentioned in the body (`\"and also save SHCSR\"`), and the commit message omits the `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` test change in `zephyr/test/drivers/panic/src/panic.c`. Copy-pasteable commit messages are provided inline on `/COMMIT_MSG`. [🔗](http://go/tj/84adf0a1-0b27-4ff3-b51d-27eb83e9e93b)",
