      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two issues in `test_panic_data_write_esf`:\n\n1. **Unrelated POSIX test change (CL scope):** Setting `esf.dummy \u003d 0xdeadbeef` and asserting `pdata-\u003eposix.esf_placeholder \u003d\u003d 0xdeadbeef` under `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` tests the pre-existing `M(dummy, posix.esf_placeholder, placeholder)` (`PANIC_COPY_REGS`) path rather than the Cortex-M `IPSR` fix (`CORTEX_PANIC_SYS_REG_LIST` / `PANIC_COPY_REGS_VAL`), and can be committed independently on its own. Please move the `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` assertion addition to a separate standalone CL.\n2. **Missing test coverage for Cortex-M `IPSR`:** Before this fix, `panic_data_write_esf()` overwrote `pdata-\u003ecm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR]` with `esf-\u003ebasic.xpsr` (e.g., `0x01000000` with the Thumb bit set and exception number `0`). Please verify that `cm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR]` stores `__get_IPSR()` rather than `esf.basic.xpsr` when compiled for Cortex-M (and in the on-device `zephyr/test/hwtest/src/panic.c` fault test):\n\n```c\nZTEST(panic, test_panic_data_write_esf)\n{\n\tstruct arch_esf esf \u003d { 0 };\n\tuint8_t expected_flags \u003d IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CROS_EC_RW) ?\n\t\t\t\t\t PANIC_DATA_FLAG_RW_IMAGE :\n\t\t\t\t\t PANIC_DATA_FLAG_RO_IMAGE;\n\n#if defined(CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M)\n\t/*\n\t * Populate a non-zero stacked xPSR (Thumb bit set, IPSR \u003d 0) to\n\t * verify that cm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR] records the live\n\t * __get_IPSR() value rather than esf.basic.xpsr.\n\t */\n\tesf.basic.xpsr \u003d 0x01000000;\n#endif\n\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARM)) {\n\t\texpected_flags |\u003d PANIC_DATA_FLAG_FRAME_VALID;\n\t}\n\n\tpanic_data_write_esf(\u0026esf);\n\n\tstruct panic_data *pdata \u003d panic_get_data();\n\n\tzassert_not_null(pdata, NULL);\n\tzassert_equal(pdata-\u003emagic, PANIC_DATA_MAGIC);\n\tzassert_equal(pdata-\u003estruct_version, PANIC_DATA_VERSION);\n\tzassert_equal(pdata-\u003estruct_size, CONFIG_PANIC_DATA_SIZE);\n\tzassert_equal(pdata-\u003eflags, expected_flags);\n#if defined(CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M)\n\tzassert_equal(pdata-\u003ecm.frame[CORTEX_PANIC_FRAME_REGISTER_PSR],\n\t\t      esf.basic.xpsr);\n\tzassert_equal(pdata-\u003ecm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR], __get_IPSR());\n#endif\n}\n```\n\nAnd in `zephyr/test/hwtest/src/panic.c` (`test_panic_data`), where `udf #0` triggers a real Cortex-M fault in handler mode, please also assert that the saved exception number is non-zero (e.g. UsageFault `6` on ARMv7-M/ARMv8-M Mainline or HardFault `3` on Cortex-M0):\n\n```c\n\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M)) {\n\t\tzassert_not_equal(pdata-\u003ecm.regs[CORTEX_PANIC_REGISTER_IPSR], 0);\n\t}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/84adf0a1-0b27-4ff3-b51d-27eb83e9e93b)",
